 was a tech genius and while we were  actively hunting him down he proved time  and time again that isaac couldn't be  trusted he showed how easy it was to  manipulate the ai into doing reporting  and saying whatever he wanted it to  this is a big part of how theo's special  tech the decoy works  following on from theo's death kina or  whoever we were fighting showed again  how easy it was to control isaac by  having it relay anything that he wanted  it to straight into our earpieces  it's entirely possible that theo and  kina had orchestrated the whole plan  that we the agents were meant to catch  up with kino on the island and take him  down  or at least think we had  so what was the point in faking his  death  to buy himself some time similar to what  he did on the west side piers  to create a distraction while he  continued with his plans except through  having everyone think he was dead the  division and black tusk would no longer  be looking for him turning their  complete attention on each other  perhaps things were getting a little too  hot for him after his betrayal of the  black tusk and this was his contingency  plan to get the heat off his back and  the only other person that knew of this  was theo which is why keena was happy to  let him die at the hands of the division  from here keena may be continuing to  build his network of rogues  when you think about it we've only met  so many so far there are likely hundreds  if not thousands more of them out there  don't get me wrong i'm really not a fan  of the whole surprise he isn't dead idea  but i certainly wouldn't be upset if  keena comes back into the picture he was  definitely one of the more interesting  characters of the story and this could  help us understand the unusual  directions character took at the end  there  but if they do go down this path they'd  have to do it right because personally  and i know for a lot of others too this  could break the immersion of the story  if it was done half-assed  there are a number of holes in the story  that would need to be plugged in order  to have this work  so perhaps this hidden alliance is  between kina and the division  he was always more aware of what was  going on in the government than the rest  of us and about the black tusk and their  motives  maybe now that the shd is finally caught  up with what is happening it is now time  for kinah to resurface and bring them in  on his plans  [Music]  as i said at the beginning i think the  most likely direction this will go will  be around natalya the black tusk and  their alliance with the hunters  i think this season will be one that is  centered around the hunters  it's likely we'll be receiving a lot  more information about them and their  origins though not everything there will  still be an air of mystery around them  this also doesn't confirm to me that the  hunters are black tusk just that they're  working with them  the leading argument is still that they  potentially have origins in russia in  some form  anyway i think i've been down the rabbit  hole for long enough now so i think i'll  wrap this one up before i completely  lose the plot on the plus side hopefully  this has helped refresh your memory on  some of what has happened in the story  up until now  thank you very much for watching and  i'll catch in the next one cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

